king what it says there.\n\nUnder the essay's recipe, distinct inputs mean distinct nodes, and in a Prisoner's Dilemma defecting dominates for any belief about the other copy, so A-FDT would submit. I'm weighing whether the inputs being functionally identical up to renaming could collapse them into one node, but the essay's red/green example treats them as separate, so I'll go with submitting.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working out how to decide under A-FDT as the essay interprets it: the twin Prisoner's Dilemma, where the other copy has different inputs (a different name and lead). Under that reading I'd intervene only on my node for Sasha's input and hold the other copy's node at its prior, unless the inputs differ only in irrelevant details, which would make the dependence subjunctive. Section 6(c) seems to address the case of different inputs, so I'm checking what it says there.\n\nUnder the essay's recipe, distinct inputs mean distinct nodes, and in a Prisoner's Dilemma defecting dominates for any belief about the other copy, so A-FDT would submit. I'm weighing whether the inputs being functionally identical up to renaming could collapse them into one node, but the essay's red/green example treats them as separate, so I'll go with submitting.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9067,"completion_tokens":784,"total_tokens":9851,"cost":0.051948,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.051948,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.036268,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01568},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":350,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}